up-right.prompt:
Use case: precise-object-edit. Sprite-animation correction.
Image 1 = approved DOWN-RIGHT walking motion reference, seven approved poses with empty cell4.
Image 2 = target WALK UP-RIGHT rear diagonal farmer, 8 poses in 4x2 layout.
Redraw BOTH ARMS in Image 2 to reproduce a real alternating walk cycle from Image 1. Current target is wrong: its far arm stays down and near arm barely changes, which must NOT be preserved. Preserve target farmer's rear-facing hat, head, torso proportions, white shirt, blue overalls and leg/boot poses. Only replace both arm/hand animations.
Analyze reference poses1 and5: they show OPPOSITE arm positions. Translate this clear front-versus-back sweep into the rear diagonal perspective, do not merely wiggle fingers. Near arm is anatomical RIGHT, near, shoulder on screen-right; far arm is anatomical LEFT, far, shoulder on screen-left. They must sweep in opposite phase. FORWARD relative to this facing is screen-right and slightly upward; BACKWARD is screen-left and downward, alongside the back of the overalls. The projected arms can overlap the torso; this is what creates real swing. Do not keep both arms splayed out toward their own screen edges.
Eight ordered poses, row-major:
1 near arm at backward extreme, far arm at forward extreme;
2 near arm beginning forward, far arm beginning backward;
3 both arms passing beneath their own shoulders;
4 near arm moving forward, far arm moving backward;
5 near arm at forward extreme, far arm at backward extreme;
6 near arm beginning backward, far arm beginning forward;
7 both arms passing beneath their own shoulders;
8 near arm moving backward, far arm moving forward, close to1 but not identical.
Use the approved reference's relaxed elbow flex, small connected palms, consistent sleeve widths, and compact hands. Near forearm at pose5 must point toward the facing, unlike pose1 which trails behind. Far forearm must also visibly reverse between1 and5. Hands follow elbows continuously, not disappear/reappear and not wave sideways. Small partial occlusion by body is fine but keep continuity and shoulder ownership. Opposite poses must NOT have the same arm silhouettes.
Output all8 finished poses, exactly4columns2rows equallyspaced transparent cells. Crisp simple pixel art, same scale across poses, enough transparent gutter. No labels, props, ground or background.

